ltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T09:05:36-07:00","id":1492304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492196-trinity-continuum-brave-new-worlds?p=1492263#post1492263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it will talk about alternate realities akin to Fringe and the like.\ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div>A book on alternate histories and realities would be fun. One for Trinity and one for the WoD.<br /> <br /> And toss in a crossover too. The Council of Nine would love to team up with the Pics Orders to kick the Aliens and Aberrants around. And the Novas could tag team against the Camarilla with the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 09-04-2022, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T19:17:44-07:00","id":1492329,"title":"","content":"I've had this long running concept for an alternate 1940s or 50s setting in which Imperial Germany won the Great War relatively quickly, with Britain never getting involved and Lenin never coming to power in Russia. I'm thinking it might work well as either a sort of diesel-tech sci-fi action thing for TC or a sort of diesel-punk noir thing for Assassins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T21:59:57-07:00","id":1492342,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm hoping we get this and the Talent player's guide soon. Between psions and aberrant, they need some more love.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T23:09:35-07:00","id":1492343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492196-trinity-continuum-brave-new-worlds?p=1492342#post1492342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm hoping we get this and the Talent player's guide soon. Between psions and aberrant, they need some more love.</div> </div> </div> </div>BNW will be a while, since it's still in first drafts. The Player's Guide will be sooner, being in manuscript approvals, though that's still on the order of several months at least.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T23:46:54-07:00","id":1492346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492196-trinity-continuum-brave-new-worlds?p=1492329#post1492329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had this long-running concept for an alternate 1940s or 50s setting in which Imperial Germany won the Great War relatively quickly, with Britain never getting involved and Lenin never coming to power in Russia. I'm thinking it might work well as either a sort of diesel-tech sci-fi action thing for TC or a sort of diesel-punk noir thing for Assassins.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you heard about Kaiserreich? <a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/...iserreich_Wiki</a> or Carbon Grey? <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Grey\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Grey</a> I often considered using these settings for an Adventure! game. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 09-05-2022, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T17:21:36-07:00","id":1492403,"title":"","content":"I like that we are getting more books for the Core and I hope we get more. I also hope the Player's Guide includes lots of options and examples of using Inspiration and Dramatic Editing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T22:27:15-07:00","id":1492416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492196-trinity-continuum-brave-new-worlds?p=1492346#post1492346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Have you heard about Kaiserreich? <a href=\"https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/The_Kaiserreich_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">https://kaiserreich.fandom.com/wiki/...iserreich_Wiki</a> or Carbon Grey? <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Grey\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Grey</a> I often considered using these settings for an Adventure! game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm vaguely aware of the Kaiserreich mod from some YouTube videos, though I don't play Hearts of Iron. The comic I have not heard of but it looks interesting.<br /> <br /> I am mainly aiming at a setting that would get rid of Lenin-Stalinism and German National Socialism, as well as Wilsonian progressive-statism. The divergence point would likely be around 1900, possibly the result of various inspired people behind the scenes. Imperial Germany never pursues a navel arms race with Britain, lowering tensions between the two, and instead spending the money on the army and other things. They don't go through Belgium to attack France, so Britain has no need to enter the war. Paris is surrounded and France surrenders, trading some of its colonial territory for peace. The Central Powers then turn East, defeating Russia. A number of puppet states (Finland, Lithuania, Ukraine, etc.) are created as a buffer zone, while the Tzar is overthrown but there is no second (Communist) revolution. Japan will later take advantage of the weakened Russia to take part of Siberia.<br /> Meanwhile, Britain will end up in a war with the Ottomans over something, with that empire collapsing, resulting in something similar to what Britain promised its Arab allies in WW1 before reneging so they could split everything with France. Also probably an independent Kurdistan and a much larger un-genocided Armenia. And at some point in the 30s, Britain will turn India into a Dominion as part of a transition to self rule. <br /> Woodrow Wilson doesn't get reelected to a second term, but I'm not sure who gets elected instead. This world avoids the Great Depression. I'm not quite sure what else is different yet. If doing this as a TC setting, it is mainly a brighter world without many of the 20th century's darker shadows looming over it. If adjusted for Assassins, t would likely focus on what it takes to keep those shadows at bay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-06T18:30:34-07:00","id":1492471,"title":"","content":"This sounds awesome! It\u2019ll be a sight to see...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}